      "urn": "urn:cts:copticLit:nt.john.bohairic:14",
      "dialect": "bohairic"
    },
    {
      "coptic": "ⲡⲇⲓⲁⲥⲧⲏⲙⲁ ⲅⲁⲣ ⲉⲧⲟⲩⲧⲱⲟⲩ ϣⲁϥⲣϩⲙⲉⲧⲏ ⲙ**ⲙⲟⲛⲏ** · ⲙⲁⲗⲓⲥⲧⲁ ⲇⲁⲛⲓⲏⲗ ⲉϥⲙⲡⲉⲥⲏⲧ ⲙⲡϣⲏⲓ ⲉϥⲟ ⲛϩⲣⲉ ⲛⲛⲉⲑⲏⲣⲓⲟⲛ ·",
      "english": "though there was a difference between them—for one used to rule in the palace—especially the case of Daniel; when he was down in the pit (and was intended) to become food for the wild beasts,",
      "source": "Instructions of Apa Pachomius in MERC.AR in Budge ed. - part 1",
      "urn": "urn:cts:copticLit:pachomius.instructions.budge:1-34",
      "dialect": "sahidic"
